{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1794182355,"nonce":"rbm+Yj1R0zToU2rB9UAxOEiKRbQ=","message":"Cost of PR 71's restyle, measured (release build, this Mac, cn stylesheet, rows of card + text + badge + button + checkbox + switch, a VisualOnly update that changes one swatch's colour, mean of 40):\n- 153 nodes: incremental_update 0.85 ms; apply_stylesheet_base_styles 2.6 ms\n- 753 nodes: incremental_update 4.3 ms; apply_stylesheet_base_styles 13.4 ms\n- 3003 nodes: incremental_update 17.6 ms; apply_stylesheet_base_styles 55.0 ms\nThe restyle is linear, about 17 to 18 us per node, and about 3x the update itself. On a 750-node screen it adds a whole 60 Hz frame to every update that takes the VisualOnly path (rebuild-triggering state changes, not signal property writes). Phones are slower still.\nSuggestion for the PR: restyle only the nodes whose props incremental_update replaced (it knows them; apply_stylesheet_base_styles_for_subtree already exists), so the cost follows the change, not the tree. Side finding: incremental_update itself is about 5.8 us per node, which is high for a diff that changed one colour.","files":null}]}